messages[12]{user,text}:
  user_1,[00:00] Hi Anita, it's Dev. I wanted to check if we can extend the travel policy that's ending on 30/09/2026.
  user_2,[00:05] Hello Dev, umm... I’m sorry, but once the policy hits the expiry date it just lapses. We can’t extend it past the 30th.
  user_1,[00:12] Oh—so it just... expires? No refund?
  user_2,[00:15] Yeah, it will be marked “Expired” in the system, and there’s no cash back. [sighs] We can only issue a fresh policy for the next travel period.
  user_1,[00:22] Got it. Would that be starting 01/10/2026 then?
  user_2,[00:24] Exactly. I can send you a quote for a new 2026‑2027 travel plan, same coverage, same premium as before, if you like.
  user_1,[00:30] That would be helpful. Can you also tell me if there’s any way to keep the same policy number? I kinda like the reference.
  user_2,[00:33] Unfortunately the old number retires with the expired policy. The new one gets a fresh ID. I know it’s a hassle.
  user_1,[00:40] Alright, I’ll review the quote. When would the new policy become active? Immediately on 01/10?
  user_2,[00:43] Yes, as soon as you accept the quote and we get payment, it’ll be active from 01/10/2026. Anything else I can help with?
  user_1,[00:48] No, that’s all. Thanks, Anita.
  user_2,[00:50] You’re welcome, Dev. Have a great day!